#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059772 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059581 :question/id #uuid "2ff0a6f5-f3b2-5b39-8b69-1a0c969548cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-4694" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n![](images/82/82729e1d34174d58f01547b58aa63db28ec68a4e1964ef5cd127a2167ed4a722.png) \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c27a3f3c-77c7-55e9-8714-1f24c4a48063" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050765 :topic/math-academy-id 148 :topic/title "Systems of Equations as Augmented Matrices"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41036779-8884-58ba-a52a-187ec59149c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236231} {:answer/id #uuid "524035f0-b03f-50f7-9a6c-85d843872657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236337} {:answer/id #uuid "ad326773-ff13-534e-8509-6da366e37306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236920} {:answer/id #uuid "d6db9a07-407a-56d4-9a6b-716466b733e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237177} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ddcfed-b7f1-5a02-8226-faae52c986bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad326773-ff13-534e-8509-6da366e37306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236920} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d34fd5-89b5-526e-b7a7-ac7984b3ddb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237653}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00a500f4-f378-5f41-9cd3-c3d0604af452" :question/math-academy-id "q-10217" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5+(-1)(5) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(-1) & 1+(-1)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f1ad10-af76-57c6-940f-54720a66b04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 8 & 12 & 14\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056138} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6b2671-bf35-5e2b-8ae2-6ed3f7c4f920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 12 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 24 & 28\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056139} {:answer/id #uuid "e2588b59-90ef-5467-875e-c92359e99c71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056140} {:answer/id #uuid "0df38360-a680-533c-85cb-cbf6cc1b956d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056141} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc99020-ce13-5c21-9960-e34814529660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056142}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5993af-0e10-5818-81f9-6717646c2956" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056137}] :question/id #uuid "afe0707b-0259-50d7-a719-7a8d24334500" :question/math-academy-id "q-10252" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A$, given by\n$A = \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]$.\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=2R_{1}$ on $A$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d500c09-be89-583e-9e7e-72a524f28363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263810} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb13c26-f7a7-5dad-b6a2-9be9b73aa159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263828} {:answer/id #uuid "6d610375-2bf0-5cef-9d1c-7da845f2aece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263948} {:answer/id #uuid "a974f595-cd6b-5b5a-9845-0ea11de039af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264448} {:answer/id #uuid "bd12ade3-f67a-5e97-b1c6-bbbec107e0be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd12ade3-f67a-5e97-b1c6-bbbec107e0be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264641} :answer-field/id #uuid "21e9df06-4ceb-5344-9619-cdc4b1c38a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "926d4b45-89b4-5d26-9733-b0d97c69c160" :question/math-academy-id "q-130070" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6efbd8af-10b5-53c6-857e-b823622056a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263962} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6b89e1-6402-52a9-b448-8fa56de1c9cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264202} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1fa668-8238-5411-8f92-5693201d70e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264355} {:answer/id #uuid "c043b83a-ecdb-5690-bcb9-8317f969f29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264672} {:answer/id #uuid "d32e7d42-9a50-5b42-b498-3e00947b27f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c043b83a-ecdb-5690-bcb9-8317f969f29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264672} :answer-field/id #uuid "54ad4053-e7d1-5505-b41b-3448a4f4c97b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265396}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25230851-35bf-5052-9d49-2045d4671518" :question/math-academy-id "q-130072" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47342003-0f7a-57c7-8078-e0f5b89cbe17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339758} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4e65ba-c319-5c08-b0e3-c9aebf3725a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339797} {:answer/id #uuid "aa16b685-af65-56c2-863d-85ebb28720ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340679} {:answer/id #uuid "ac12c08c-7cda-5cfc-92cd-fec65f15dc5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340698} {:answer/id #uuid "d50c28fb-2517-5de6-83c6-0fda23c711b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa16b685-af65-56c2-863d-85ebb28720ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340679} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f29d7cf-1107-533f-a29c-b3d47d877104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341519}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7de40719-e1b7-5230-a137-1dc3c55de0ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-72763" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(3)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "059aa882-887d-5963-939d-82931aef6767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339173} {:answer/id #uuid "4b0bec89-af06-5c39-a6ae-0b90c1b29c8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339802} {:answer/id #uuid "5eeb714f-153e-596d-a218-51cd00bee02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339971} {:answer/id #uuid "6a24ab21-f606-59a2-ae94-25e33a5c5d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340069} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2c9e9c-f924-5be6-803e-89dd2685301d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5eeb714f-153e-596d-a218-51cd00bee02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339971} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d01fb6-6a2b-5600-96a6-bbb4758f192b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341576}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4f7e0cb8-b82b-5c57-8695-0b8e08268369" :question/math-academy-id "q-72786" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1 & -3+0 & 4+3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5228249-42b4-5b6c-a34b-688628cf3c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -\\frac{8}{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388071} {:answer/id #uuid "0df908b7-b9cf-5d37-aca8-7f00b46a2051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388072} {:answer/id #uuid "afd3402b-d0f0-5d8e-92cd-42bc4ac1d793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388073} {:answer/id #uuid "269dae98-aadc-597a-82e7-371420d4533a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388074} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee9af5a-41eb-5f3b-a278-9fcb76973748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afd3402b-d0f0-5d8e-92cd-42bc4ac1d793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388073} :answer-field/id #uuid "95465894-f1f7-5a8d-84b8-f2ad025aafe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388070}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f08a2c2-eb16-5d85-a714-beb36e4a0c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-130071" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:=(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 6 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (-3) & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 9 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6756ed00-330f-5c8c-8a4d-fbb86cdc2c8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393224} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfcb35e-95c9-5403-a320-dcd7face84d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -4\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393225} {:answer/id #uuid "d3557d97-0c1d-5853-b9fd-91ee81522e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393226} {:answer/id #uuid "7936a577-d3bd-55bd-b9c4-bfcbd8d64f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393227} {:answer/id #uuid "3c473b8d-8970-5a89-afb6-b17390deb661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c473b8d-8970-5a89-afb6-b17390deb661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393228} :answer-field/id #uuid "43860d4a-16fb-54d3-8d76-5164ce10d9b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393223}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e529998-60b8-53c0-bae5-50351fb55c46" :question/math-academy-id "q-72757" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ on $T?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2+(2)(1) & -2+(2)(3) & 1+(2)(2)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76e35e5d-3d96-5355-b632-9dcb08a7d598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393231} {:answer/id #uuid "37c197ca-a8a9-536c-8b89-25989a9a892c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393232} {:answer/id #uuid "3f1549bb-38c0-5786-af6b-6a9b6ef9bf0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref